  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_037, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.706) establishes that multiprofile, avgpool aggregation, weighted fusion, and imagenet_vit_l are all beneficial. The RNA encoder has shown the largest single-variable gain (pca→scvi_n200 gave +0.039), but scgpt has never been tested in any multimodal setting. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder when paired with the best image encoder and aggregation/fusion settings? This experiment isolates the RNA encoder variable by holding all other settings at their empirically best values (multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted). Why this is the best next experiment: It tests the highest-impact unexplored design choice in the strongest known configuration. A direct comparison with config_037 cleanly attributes any difference to the RNA encoder. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 and redirects budget toward other levers (e.g., transformer aggregation at the top level or singleprofile trade-offs). Under a limited budget, resolving this key uncertainty is more valuable than testing a lower-impact variation like transformer aggregation, which has consistently underperformed avgpool."
}

